---
title: Card Servicing logical architecture
config:
  flowchart:
    rankSpacing: 350
    curve: monotoneX
---
flowchart LR
    CardServicingUi["Deferred account servicing UI"]
    ApiGateway["TLS ingress and routing"]
    CardServicingService["Balance and transaction API"]
    AuthService["Token and access decisions"]
    ConfigService["Paging and timeout settings"]
    AzureManagedRedis[("Read-through response cache")]
    FixtureLoader["Loads fixture data"]
    CardDataService["Account and balance data"]
    TransactionActivityService["Transaction history"]
    ReferenceDataService["Type and category descriptions"]
    AzureKeyVault["Deployed secret source"]
    AzurePostgres[("Stub mock-data store")]

    subgraph Legend["Legend"]
        LegendCompute["Compute"]
        LegendDataStores["Data stores"]
        LegendExternal["External systems"]
        LegendSecurity["Security"]
        LegendNetworking["Networking"]
    end

    CardServicingUi -->|HTTPS REST| ApiGateway
    ApiGateway -->|REST or gRPC| CardServicingService
    CardServicingService -->|gRPC| AuthService
    CardServicingService -->|gRPC| CardDataService
    CardServicingService -->|gRPC| TransactionActivityService
    CardServicingService -->|gRPC| ReferenceDataService
    CardServicingService -->|gRPC| ConfigService
    CardServicingService -->|cache read-write| AzureManagedRedis
    %% Every component that reads a deployed secret (service API key, Redis or database password) reads it from Key Vault, as the TRD environment-variable table lists.
    CardServicingService -->|secret read| AzureKeyVault
    FixtureLoader -->|secret read| AzureKeyVault
    CardDataService -->|secret read| AzureKeyVault
    TransactionActivityService -->|secret read| AzureKeyVault
    ReferenceDataService -->|secret read| AzureKeyVault
    FixtureLoader -->|fixture load| AzurePostgres
    CardDataService -->|table read| AzurePostgres
    TransactionActivityService -->|table read| AzurePostgres
    ReferenceDataService -->|table read| AzurePostgres

    classDef compute fill:#add8e6,stroke:#333333,color:#000000
    classDef datastore fill:#90ee90,stroke:#333333,color:#000000
    classDef external fill:#d3d3d3,stroke:#333333,color:#000000
    classDef security fill:#f4cccc,stroke:#333333,color:#000000
    classDef networking fill:#ffffe0,stroke:#333333,color:#000000

    class CardServicingUi,ApiGateway,CardServicingService,FixtureLoader,LegendCompute compute
    class AzurePostgres,AzureManagedRedis,LegendDataStores datastore
    class CardDataService,TransactionActivityService,ConfigService,ReferenceDataService,AuthService,LegendExternal external
    class AzureKeyVault,LegendSecurity security
    class LegendNetworking networking

    style Legend fill:#ffffff,stroke:#333333
    Description["The Card Servicing service answers UI balance and drill-down requests by calling five stubbed external systems over gRPC, asking the Auth stub for every token and account-access decision and caching in Redis only account, category-balance, transaction and reference-data answers plus the Config snapshot mirror. The Card Data, Transaction Activity and Reference Data stubs read the fixture data that the loader writes to PostgreSQL."]
